│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  1. Validate the remaining length before every subtraction in both tuple     │
│  loops: reject the packet when fewer than the 2-byte topic length plus the   │
│  1-byte QoS level (SUBSCRIBE) or fewer than the 2-byte topic length          │
│  (UNSUBSCRIBE) remain, and reject it again when the declared topic length    │
│  exceeds what is left after the topic length field has been consumed.        │
│  Reject before reading the packet identifier when the declared length        │
│  cannot hold it plus at least one complete tuple.                            │
│  2. Make the loop counter itself trustworthy: derive each iteration's bound  │
│  from the bytes actually present in the packet rather than from the          │
│  declared length alone, and fail closed on any packet whose contents do not  │
│  exactly match its declared length.                                          │
│  3. Remove the unreachable error branch or make the allocation helper        │
│  return an error instead of terminating the process, so that a decode        │
│  failure costs one connection rather than the whole broker.                  │
│  4. Reject and discard decoded packets that failed validation: the caller    │
│  currently ignores the decoder's return code and dispatches the partially    │
│  populated packet to the command handlers, which then operate on an empty    │
│  tuple list.                                                                 │
│  5. Bound the tuple count to the 16-bit field that stores it, and free the   │
│  tuples already decoded when validation fails so that malformed packets      │
│  cannot leak memory.                                                         │
│  6. Apply the same availability-before-subtraction rule to the remaining     │
│  length arithmetic in the PUBLISH and CONNECT decoders, which use the same   │
│  pattern.                                                                    │
│  7. Add regression tests that feed each decoder truncated and                │
│  length-inconsistent packets and assert a clean protocol error plus a live   │
│  broker process.                                                             │
│                                                                              │
